{"path":"coroutine/generator/~generator","title":"std::generator<Ref,V,Allocator>::~generator","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::generator&lt;Ref,V,Allocator&gt;::</span>~generator","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/coroutine/generator/~generator","section":"coroutine","kind":"page","summary":"Destructs the generator object.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">~generator<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Destructs the generator object.\n</p><p>Given <a href=\"/w/cpp/coroutine/generator#Data_members\"><code><i>coroutine_</i></code></a> as the underlying coroutine object, equivalent to:\n</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>coroutine_<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    coroutine_.<span class=\"me1\">destroy</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></code></pre>\n<p>Note, that destroying the root generator effectively destroys the entire stack of yielded generators, because the ownership of recursively yielded generators is held in awaitable objects in the coroutine frame of the yielding generator. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete </div>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"coroutine","title":"Coroutine support (C++20)"},{"path":"coroutine/generator","title":"std::generator"}],"ch